{"parentUuid":"84d82a56-f281-4018-adc5-62d40dfa5e94","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_017hq8BNa2cmtsN7U6uQu6xd","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"additionalContext\":\"<context_guidance>\\n  <tip>\\n    When you intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries) for multiple commands or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"javascript\\\", code: \\\"...\\\") for one — the raw output stays in the sandbox and only what you print enters your conversation. Shell stays the right surface when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation); if you use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"shell\\\"), write syntax for the host shell.\\n  </tip>\\n</context_guidance>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.mjs\"","durationMs":102},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d5b6a9d1-bec9-49ec-b4d7-6dfa7564b88d","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:00:34.139Z","session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
