{"parentUuid":"e8590882-2fec-45f3-8dbb-9381be5ad466","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1a9e6a61-377c-4fad-af18-9476f244b7f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XycL3KafG1dRxyQUUaUadj","type":"tool_result","content":"on it several times and was not sure what was left.\n\n## What we found\nThe disk side was already done. All 130 top-level DEV repos, 13 under Football/, and 2\nunder SpecialRequests/ had GitHub remotes, zero uncommitted changes, zero unpushed\ncommits. The remaining work was smaller than expected.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Duplicate clone folders.** `Gemini Projects` and `Website` were byte-identical clones\nat the same commit as `Gemini_Projects` and `AppliedPerformance-Site`, each pair sharing\none remote. Two folders pointing at one remote is how work gets lost. Kept the folder\nmatching the remote name, moved the other to `_to_delete/2026-09-14_dup_clones/`.\n\n**Codex scratch sweep.** `~/Documents/Codex` held 11 date-stamped folders that Codex\ncreates when a session starts outside a project directory. Nine were empty or throwaway.\nSalvaged and pushed:\n\n| From | To |\n|---|---|\n| 2026-09-03 | `PP_Recruiting/scripts/agm_summary/{build,restyle}_agm_summary.py`, `PP_Recruiting/docs/agm_summary_artifact.md` |\n| 2026-08-03 | `Baylor_Doc_Style/scripts/logo/` (4 .py), `Baylor_Doc_Style/assets/logo/` (3 .png) |\n| 2026-08-05 | `TechEd_Prop/ShitfWave/assests/{Baylor-x-Shiftwave.jpg,jpeg-import-qa.pptx}` |\n| 2026-08-07 | `_DRIVE/00_INBOX/Personal/Olivia_Birthday_Invitations_2-up_Duplex.pdf` |\n| 2026-08-06 | `agent-skills/_recovered-from-codex/` (5 .py + README) |\n\n----\n---\nname: personal-site-build-routes\ndescription: \"Eric's personal site is an Artifact with hard constraints — what that forbids, why scroll-craft cannot run on it, and where the standalone build lives instead\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:38.332Z\n---\n\nTwo separate things, both under `~/DEV/Website/` (which **is** a git repo,\nremote `erash11/AppliedPerformance-Site`, though `personal/` is deliberately\nuntracked):\n\n**1. The live site — `~/DEV/Website/personal/index.html`.** Published as a Claude\nArtifact; republish with the stored `url` to keep the link. Current brief is\n`BRIEF-V3.md` (\"Night Field\", dark-first, Texas, kitsch ban) — V1 and V2 are\nsuperseded, so quote V3. Its hard rules: one Google Fonts link and **no other\nexternal resource**, no libraries, no fetch, Canvas 2D and inline SVG only,\nnothing readable parked at `opacity: 0`, `prefers-reduced-motion` fully usable.\n\n**These constraints structurally forbid scroll-craft**, which needs an engine\nJS/CSS pair on disk, external video, and scroll-assembled text. It is not a\ntuning problem; the two cannot both be satisfied. Anything premium wanted on the\nArtifact has to be hand-built inline: layering via transforms, stacking cards,\ncounting numbers.\n\n**2. The standalone build — `~/DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`.**\nEric's chosen answer (2026-09-02). A real scroll-craft build, split-stage\ngrammar, no video, all visuals code-drawn. Serve it:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash\nnode ~/.agents/skills/scroll-craft/scripts/serve.mjs --root . --port 4500\n```\n\nNot hosted, and it does not touch the Artifact. `lab/` holds a few hundred\nverification PNGs and is gitignored; it reached 339MB in one session, so never\nstage it.\n\n**Before critiquing his site, read it.** It already leads with the problem\n(\"Most performance problems are not data problems. They are question problems.\")\nand already has a scroll-driven jump-trace scrub. Assuming otherwise produced a\nwrong claim that had to be retracted.\n\nRedesign notes live in `~/DEV/Website/personal/DESIGN-IDEAS.md`.\nRelated: [[vendored-skill-install]], [[dev-layout-and-discovery]].\n\n- **Cowork install route (2026-09-02):** Claude Code and Codex load scroll-craft directly. Cowork cannot; it needs the skill uploaded as a zip from `~/Downloads`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b6cb975a-9bc9-4dd8-9903-0520c2bd6542","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:02:57.278Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"on it several times and was not sure what was left.\n\n## What we found\nThe disk side was already done. All 130 top-level DEV repos, 13 under Football/, and 2\nunder SpecialRequests/ had GitHub remotes, zero uncommitted changes, zero unpushed\ncommits. The remaining work was smaller than expected.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Duplicate clone folders.** `Gemini Projects` and `Website` were byte-identical clones\nat the same commit as `Gemini_Projects` and `AppliedPerformance-Site`, each pair sharing\none remote. Two folders pointing at one remote is how work gets lost. Kept the folder\nmatching the remote name, moved the other to `_to_delete/2026-09-14_dup_clones/`.\n\n**Codex scratch sweep.** `~/Documents/Codex` held 11 date-stamped folders that Codex\ncreates when a session starts outside a project directory. Nine were empty or throwaway.\nSalvaged and pushed:\n\n| From | To |\n|---|---|\n| 2026-09-03 | `PP_Recruiting/scripts/agm_summary/{build,restyle}_agm_summary.py`, `PP_Recruiting/docs/agm_summary_artifact.md` |\n| 2026-08-03 | `Baylor_Doc_Style/scripts/logo/` (4 .py), `Baylor_Doc_Style/assets/logo/` (3 .png) |\n| 2026-08-05 | `TechEd_Prop/ShitfWave/assests/{Baylor-x-Shiftwave.jpg,jpeg-import-qa.pptx}` |\n| 2026-08-07 | `_DRIVE/00_INBOX/Personal/Olivia_Birthday_Invitations_2-up_Duplex.pdf` |\n| 2026-08-06 | `agent-skills/_recovered-from-codex/` (5 .py + README) |\n\n----\n---\nname: personal-site-build-routes\ndescription: \"Eric's personal site is an Artifact with hard constraints — what that forbids, why scroll-craft cannot run on it, and where the standalone build lives instead\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:38.332Z\n---\n\nTwo separate things, both under `~/DEV/Website/` (which **is** a git repo,\nremote `erash11/AppliedPerformance-Site`, though `personal/` is deliberately\nuntracked):\n\n**1. The live site — `~/DEV/Website/personal/index.html`.** Published as a Claude\nArtifact; republish with the stored `url` to keep the link. Current brief is\n`BRIEF-V3.md` (\"Night Field\", dark-first, Texas, kitsch ban) — V1 and V2 are\nsuperseded, so quote V3. Its hard rules: one Google Fonts link and **no other\nexternal resource**, no libraries, no fetch, Canvas 2D and inline SVG only,\nnothing readable parked at `opacity: 0`, `prefers-reduced-motion` fully usable.\n\n**These constraints structurally forbid scroll-craft**, which needs an engine\nJS/CSS pair on disk, external video, and scroll-assembled text. It is not a\ntuning problem; the two cannot both be satisfied. Anything premium wanted on the\nArtifact has to be hand-built inline: layering via transforms, stacking cards,\ncounting numbers.\n\n**2. The standalone build — `~/DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`.**\nEric's chosen answer (2026-09-02). A real scroll-craft build, split-stage\ngrammar, no video, all visuals code-drawn. Serve it:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash\nnode ~/.agents/skills/scroll-craft/scripts/serve.mjs --root . --port 4500\n```\n\nNot hosted, and it does not touch the Artifact. `lab/` holds a few hundred\nverification PNGs and is gitignored; it reached 339MB in one session, so never\nstage it.\n\n**Before critiquing his site, read it.** It already leads with the problem\n(\"Most performance problems are not data problems. They are question problems.\")\nand already has a scroll-driven jump-trace scrub. Assuming otherwise produced a\nwrong claim that had to be retracted.\n\nRedesign notes live in `~/DEV/Website/personal/DESIGN-IDEAS.md`.\nRelated: [[vendored-skill-install]], [[dev-layout-and-discovery]].\n\n- **Cowork install route (2026-09-02):** Claude Code and Codex load scroll-craft directly. Cowork cannot; it needs the skill uploaded as a zip from `~/Downloads`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e8590882-2fec-45f3-8dbb-9381be5ad466","session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
