{"parentUuid":"52a53c50-d820-4603-b512-e2cf393a1ee5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d061284d-0f36-4477-b5cb-9d75fc514cb1","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:18:06.633Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d061284d-0f36-4477-b5cb-9d75fc514cb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf83wRrNCcLxqhEHGdWtm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Memsearch was never broken. The crash happened because the Mac was restarting when a session ended.\n\n- **Cause:** The crash was at 07:46:41, and the Mac restarted at 07:46:56. During shutdown, macOS stops programs from loading new libraries. Memsearch showed that as \"requires onnxruntime, pip install\", which was wrong. The install is fine, so do not reinstall it.\n- **Why it looked worse:** The hook (the script that re-indexes when a session ends) saved only the first 300 characters of the error. The real message, \"system is shutting down\", was cut off.\n- **Fix:** I changed `~/.claude/hooks/memsearch-sync.js`:\n  - A crash during shutdown now counts as a short-term problem. It raises an alert only after 6 failed runs in a row, the same as timeouts.\n  - Other errors still raise an alert. The alert now shows the real error line and where the full log is.\n  - The Codex copy links to this file, so Codex gets the fix too.\n- **Check:**\n  - I tested the change on today's real crash output. The crash was matched, and other errors still get reported.\n  - A real run of the hook indexed 4 chunks with no new errors.\n- **Commit:** `2ed1e54` in `~/.claude`, pushed.\n\nThe old 07:46 memsearch line is still in `.errors.log`, so you will see it again at the next session start. I did not clear it, because the log also holds the GPS error and the backup error.\n\nresult: The memsearch crash was a Mac restart, not a broken install. The hook no longer alerts on a crash during shutdown and now logs the real cause (`~/.claude` commit `2ed1e54`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":125524,"output_tokens":554,"output_tokens_details":{