{"parentUuid":"81a90a9a-9f5a-4107-84da-a88c9e6be160","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"087e126b-996a-4039-aa74-d34f58a235be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018L8Q9JawsXnE8ohNprdWuH","type":"tool_result","content":"20\t  2026-09-12 built HTML + PDF. `pull.sh` by hand from `/tmp`: exit 0, 17 skipped, no alerts.\n21\t  `com.keystone.gpspull` installed and bootstrapped (daily 06:30). Codex: plan APPROVED (round 6); code\n22\t  inspected 3× (all REVISE, every finding fixed); the inspection-3 fixes and a later test-isolation fix are\n23\t  not Codex-inspected (Eric's override).\n24\t\n25\t## Next\n26\t- Done 2026-09-13, verified on Windows: the only task running `refresh_all_data.bat` is `\\Refresh_All_Data`\n27\t  (`_INBOX` copy, GPS step REM'd). No Windows task runs `bulk_import.py`. See\n28\t  `_INBOX/docs/handoffs/2026-09-13-windows-sync-refresh-task.md`.\n29\t- Check the first scheduled run after 06:30: `gps_report/logs/last_run.json` (status ok, `run_id` set) and\n30\t  `gps_report/logs/launchd-gpspull.log`.\n31\t- Optional follow-up: have `claude-stack-doctor` read `last_run.json` too.\n32\t\n33\t## Open questions\n34\t- Rotate the Catapult token (plain text in `.env`, the CLI credentials, Drive `Bearer.txt`, and git\n35\t  history `91a233b`)? Eric's call.\n36\t- Rewrite git history to drop `API_Token_FB.txt`? Eric's call (repo is private).\n37\t\n38\t---\n39\t"}]},"uuid":"b1383a02-5cc9-4afd-aefe-40d2fb6195f3","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:23:44.775Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","content":"  2026-09-12 built HTML + PDF. `pull.sh` by hand from `/tmp`: exit 0, 17 skipped, no alerts.\n  `com.keystone.gpspull` installed and bootstrapped (daily 06:30). Codex: plan APPROVED (round 6); code\n  inspected 3× (all REVISE, every finding fixed); the inspection-3 fixes and a later test-isolation fix are\n  not Codex-inspected (Eric's override).\n\n## Next\n- Done 2026-09-13, verified on Windows: the only task running `refresh_all_data.bat` is `\\Refresh_All_Data`\n  (`_INBOX` copy, GPS step REM'd). No Windows task runs `bulk_import.py`. See\n  `_INBOX/docs/handoffs/2026-09-13-windows-sync-refresh-task.md`.\n- Check the first scheduled run after 06:30: `gps_report/logs/last_run.json` (status ok, `run_id` set) and\n  `gps_report/logs/launchd-gpspull.log`.\n- Optional follow-up: have `claude-stack-doctor` read `last_run.json` too.\n\n## Open questions\n- Rotate the Catapult token (plain text in `.env`, the CLI credentials, Drive `Bearer.txt`, and git\n  history `91a233b`)? Eric's call.\n- Rewrite git history to drop `API_Token_FB.txt`? Eric's call (repo is private).\n\n---\n","numLines":20,"startLine":20,"totalLines":59}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81a90a9a-9f5a-4107-84da-a88c9e6be160","session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b1383a02-5cc9-4afd-aefe-40d2fb6195f3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project Purpose\n\nAthletic performance data infrastructure for Baylor University. The primary active project is an automated post-practice GPS report for Football using the Catapult API. ForceDecks integration is a separate, future project.\n\n## Project: `coach_report/`\n\n**Post-session coach report** — high-level planned-vs-actual one-pager for coaches, read-only consumer of `gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` (never writes to it). Sections: planned vs actual (Player Load, PL/min, Explosive Efforts vs day-type historical IQR), max-velocity exposure lists, and XmR SPC flags for over-/under-dosed athletes with sparkline control charts. Output: self-contained HTML + PDF under `coach_report/Reports/coach/YYYY-MM-DD/`.\n\n```\ncd coach_report\npython coach_report.py --date today            # after practice (data must be ingested by gps_report first)\npython coach_report.py --date 2026-04-25       # specific date\npython -m pytest tests/                        # unit tests\n```\n\nDay-type regexes, thresholds, and SPC settings live in `coach_config.yaml`; per-date plan overrides in `plan_overrides.yaml`. Design spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-coach-report-design.md`. Note: the DB column `total_player_load` stores Catapult `average_player_load` (a per-period average; true/stored ratio varies ~5–17× by season — NOT a usable volume metric). coach_report derives **true session Player Load = `player_load_per_minute` × minutes** (verified identical to `pl_low+pl_med+pl_high+pl_veryhigh`, which is the fallback when PL/min is null); this matches AJ's team report exactly. Intensity uses stored `player_load_per_minute` (duration-weighted across multi-session days).\n\n## Active Project: `gps_report/`\n\n**Automated post-practice GPS report** — pulls Football session data from Catapult Connect v6 API, stores summary stats in DuckDB, and generates a self-contained HTML report + plain-text email summary.\n\n### Entry points\n```\ncd gps_report\n\n# Daily report (after practice)\npython run_report.py                          # interactive — picks today's session\npython run_report.py --date 2026-03-10        # specific date\npython run_report.py --session-id <uuid>      # skip picker\npython run_report.py --list-positions         # print Catapult position strings (setup)\npython run_report.py --force                  # re-import existing session\n\n# Regular pull — the one command (also runs daily at 06:30 via launchd com.keystone.gpspull)\n./pull.sh                                     # import new sessions (--since-db), then coach reports for new dates\n\n# Bulk import\npython bulk_import.py --since-db              # newest stored date − pull.overlap_days (3) → today\npython bulk_import.py                         # 2025-03-22 → today (practices, walk-thrus, games, mock games)\npython bulk_import.py --dry-run               # preview matching sessions without DB writes\npython bulk_import.py --start 2025-08-01 --end 2025-12-31\npython bulk_import.py --force                 # re-import sessions already in DB\n\n# Tests (no network, no real DB)\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q\n\n# Backfill / recompute velocity + band columns for historical sessions\npython backfill_velocity.py                   # all non-walk-through sessions\npython backfill_velocity.py --dry-run         # preview without DB writes\npython backfill_velocity.py --session-id <uuid>  # single session\n```\n\n### Session name conventions (Catapult)\n| Type | Name pattern | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Practice | standalone `P` token | `SP25 - P1 - 03.22.25`, `AUBURN - P3 - 08.26.25` |\n| Walk-thru | contains `Walk Thru` | `SP25 - Walk Thru #1 - 03.24.25` |\n| Game | standalone `G` token | `AUBURN - G1 - 08.29.25` |\n| Mock game | contains `Mock Game` → day type `scrimmage` (kept out of practice norms and practice SPC history) | `FC26 - MOCK GAME - 08.29.26` |\n\n### Install dependencies (first time only, macOS)\n```\ncd gps_report\n~/.local/bin/uv venv .venv --python 3.14\n~/.local/bin/uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements-dev.txt\n```\nNever `pip install` globally (Python is PEP 668-managed on this Mac). `pull.sh` and launchd use `gps_report/.venv/bin/python`.\n\n### Regular pull (added 2026-09-13)\n- **Owner:** the Mac owns `data/gps_history.duckdb`. The Windows `Refresh_All_Data` GPS step must stay off (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n- **Schedule:** `ops/com.keystone.gpspull.plist` → `~/Library/LaunchAgents/`, daily 06:30; launchd runs a missed job on wake from sleep, not after power-off. Logs: `gps_report/logs/launchd-gpspull.{log,err}`.\n- **Receipt:** every `bulk_import.py` run writes `logs/last_run.json` (status, exit code, window, counts, `imported_dates`, `last_success_at`). Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 usage/config/token · 2 DB open/lock · 3 partial · 4 all listing windows failed or roster fetch failed · 5 unexpected.\n- **Alerts:** `pull.sh` appends one line to `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` (surfaced at Claude Code session start) on a non-zero import, a coach report that fails or leaves no HTML/PDF, or no successful pull for 36 h.\n- **Atomic sessions:** a session's header and athlete rows commit together or not at all; any stats row without an athlete id fails the session so it is retried.\n- **Retry backlog:** the receipt's `retry_from` is the earliest date of any failed listing window or unstored session. The next `--since-db` run starts at the earlier of `newest − overlap_days` and `retry_from`, so a later success never strands an earlier failure. Only a clean `--since-db` run clears it; range and dry runs never do.\n- Plan and Codex review: `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-PLAN.md`, `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-REVIEW-LOG.md`.\n\n### Key files\n- [gps_report/run_report.py](gps_report/run_report.py) — entry point; session picker, data fetch, report render\n- [gps_report/bulk_import.py](gps_report/bulk_import.py) — bulk historical import (practices, walk-thrus, games)\n- [gps_report/config.yaml](gps_report/config.yaml) — flagging thresholds, position groups, region\n- [gps_report/.env](gps_report/.env) — `CATAPULT_TOKEN=<jwt>` (not in git)\n- [gps_report/src/api_client.py](gps_report/src/api_client.py) — Catapult Connect v6 REST client\n- [gps_report/src/storage.py](gps_report/src/storage.py) — DuckDB schema + queries\n- [gps_report/src/baseline.py](gps_report/src/baseline.py) — rolling 28-day baseline + flagging\n- [gps_report/src/report_builder.py](gps_report/src/report_builder.py) — HTML + email text generation\n- [gps_report/templates/report.html.j2](gps_report/templates/report.html.j2) — Jinja2 report template\n- [gps_report/backfill_velocity.py](gps_report/backfill_velocity.py) — re-fetch and recompute velocity + band columns for historical sessions\n\n### Architecture\n```\nPOST /stats (Catapult Connect v6)\n  └── api_client.py  →  storage.py (DuckDB)\n                              └── baseline.py  →  report_builder.py  →  Reports/YYYY-MM-DD/\n```\n\n### API details (Catapult Connect v6)\n- **Base URL:** `https://connect-us.catapultsports.com/api/v6`\n- **Auth:** JWT Bearer token in `gps_report/.env` as `CATAPULT_TOKEN`\n- **Token scope:** `connect`, `catapultr`, `sensor-read-only`\n- **Activities filter:** `start_time` / `end_time` are **Unix timestamps** (not ISO 8601)\n- **Stats endpoint:** `POST /stats` with `filters: [{name: \"activity_id\", comparison: \"=\", values: [uuid]}]`\n- **Stats source:** `cached_stats`, `group_by: [\"athlete\"]`\n- **`POST /stats` works** and returns 200 — `bake_status=unprocessed` does NOT block it\n- **Do NOT use:** `maximum_velocity`, `high_speed_running_distance`, `athlete_max_velocity`, `percentage_max_velocity`, `deceleration_density` — return 0 or wrong slugs for this account\n- **`max_vel`** = session max velocity in **mph** — multiply × 0.44704 to store as m/s\n- **`velocity_band3_total_distance`** = HSD (75–90% of max vel), in meters\n- **`velocity_band4–8_total_distance`** = sprint bands; bands 5–8 always return 0 for Baylor\n- **Full parameter list** available at `GET /parameters` — 1,829 slugs. Saved to `logs/all_parameters.json`.\n\n### Metric field mapping (API → DB)\n| API field | DB column | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `average_player_load` | `total_player_load` | session average per athlete, not cumulative |\n| `total_distance` | `total_distance_m` | stored in meters; displayed in yards |\n| `max_vel` | `max_velocity_ms` | API value is mph; stored m/s (`× 0.44704`); displayed mph |\n| `velocity_band3_total_distance` | `vb3_distance_m` + `high_speed_distance_m` | raw band stored; derived metric computed from config |\n| `velocity_band4–8_total_distance` | `vb4–vb8_distance_m` + `sprint_distance_m` | raw bands stored; derived metric summed from config |\n| `velocity_band3/4_total_effort_count` | `vb3_effort_count`, `vb4_effort_count` | # entries into HSD/sprint zones |\n| `acceleration_density` | `accel_density` | |\n| `explosive_efforts` | `explosive_efforts` | = `total_high_ima` (same values) |\n| `total_duration` | `total_duration_s` | session duration in seconds |\n| `total_acceleration_load` | `total_accel_load` | |\n| `average_velocity` | `average_velocity_ms` | stored m/s |\n| `meterage_per_minute` | `meterage_per_minute` | |\n| `player_load_per_minute` | `player_load_per_minute` | |\n| `explosive_ratio_(avg)` | `explosive_ratio_avg` | |\n| `ima_band3_accel/decel/right/left_count` | `ima_high_accel/decel/right/left` | high-intensity IMA counts |\n| `high_ima_accel/decel` | `ima_high_accel_decel` | combined high IMA accel+decel |\n| `total_high/medium/low_ima(_movements)` | `total_high/medium/low_ima` | IMA movement tier totals |\n| `ima/min`, `total_high_ima/min`, `total_high_ima_(avg)` | `ima_per_minute`, `total_high_ima_per_min`, `total_high_ima_avg` | IMA rate/avg metrics |\n| `impacts_low/med/high` | `impacts_low/med/high` | collision/contact event counts |\n| `impact_low_(avg)`, `impacts_med_(avg)`, `impacts_high_(avg)` | `impacts_low/med/high_avg` | impact averages |\n| `pl_low/med/high/veryhigh` | `pl_low/med/high/veryhigh` | player load band totals |\n| `pl_med_(avg)` | `pl_high_avg` | ⚠️ Catapult name/slug mismatch — slug says \"med\" but value is PL_High (Avg) |\n| `pl_veryhigh_(avg)`, `pl_veryhigh/min` | `pl_veryhigh_avg`, `pl_veryhigh_per_min` | |\n| `total_lineman_contact_count` | `total_contacts` | all players (not just linemen despite name) |\n| `total_qb_throw_count` | `total_throws` | QB-specific; zero for all non-QB athletes |\n\n### Velocity band storage architecture\nRaw band columns (`vb3_distance_m`–`vb8_distance_m`) are stored as DB ground truth. Derived metrics (`high_speed_distance_m`, `sprint_distance_m`) are computed at ingest from `config.yaml` `metrics.derived` band assignments — same principle as m→yds/m/s→mph unit conversions. To redefine HSD or Sprint zones: edit `config.yaml` → run `python backfill_velocity.py`. No code changes needed.\n\n### Athlete roster API fields (`GET /athletes`)\n- **Name:** `first_name` + `last_name` (separate fields — no `full_name`, `name`, or `displayName`)\n- **Jersey:** `jersey` field (string, may be non-numeric e.g. `\"DBB\"`) — parse to `int`, store `NULL` if non-numeric\n- **Position:** `position_name` (e.g. `\"DL\"`) preferred over `position` (single-letter code e.g. `\"D\"`)\n- Parsed in `parse_athlete()` in both `run_report.py` and `bulk_import.py`\n\n### Position group mapping\nRun `--list-positions` to see actual Catapult position strings. Config already updated with live values from web UI. Position names from `GET /athletes` include `position_name` field.\n\n### HTML report layout (sections, top to bottom)\n1. Header band (Baylor green) — wordmark, session name/date, athlete count\n2. Gold accent bar\n3. KPI tiles (4) — Team Avg PL · Avg Distance (yds) · Avg Max Speed mph (N/A when 0) · Avg Explosive Efforts\n4. Charts row — SVG volume trend sparkline (last 10 sessions) + Top Speeds CSS bars (top 8 by mph)\n5. Position Group Summary table — group, N, avg PL, avg dist (yds), avg speed (mph), avg HSD (yds), avg explosive; high/low cell shading\n6. Athlete Flags — card layout per athlete, HIGH (orange) / LOW (blue) badges with baseline context\n7. Offensive Breakdown — Skill, OL group player tables\n8. Defensive Breakdown — DBs, STAR, LB, DL group player tables\n9. Other — Special Teams\n10. Footer\n\n### Display units\n- **Distance:** stored in meters (DB), displayed in **yards** everywhere in report (`m_to_yds()` in `src/utils.py`)\n- **Velocity:** stored in m/s (DB), displayed in **mph** everywhere in report (`ms_to_mph()` in `src/utils.py`)\n- Do NOT change DB storage units — conversion is display-layer only\n\n### Baseline flagging\n- Activates after 3 sessions per athlete (configurable: `flagging.min_sessions_for_baseline`)\n- Default: flag if value is >1.5 SD from rolling 28-day personal average\n- Metrics flagged: Total Player Load, Total Distance, High Speed Distance\n\n### Jinja2 + pandas NA gotcha\nPandas `NA` values (from DuckDB nullable integer columns like `jersey_number`) cannot be evaluated as booleans in Jinja2 (`{% if athlete.jersey_number %}`). Always convert with `None if pd.isna(val) else val` in `report_builder.py` before passing to the template.\n\n### DuckDB lock risk\n`data/gps_history.duckdb` allows one writer. A second writer (a manual `run_report.py` or import during the 06:30 pull) fails fast with a lock error — the import exits 2 and alerts. Never put the DB in a cloud-synced folder (Google Drive / OneDrive sync locks it); it stays local and gitignored.\n\n## Architecture Decisions\n\n- **Scope:** Football GPS only — ForceDecks is a separate future project\n- **Storage:** DuckDB local file (`gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb`) — summary stats only, no raw 10Hz data\n- **API:** Catapult Connect v6 (US region); JWT token in `gps_report/.env`\n- **Scheduled pull (changed 2026-09-13, Eric):** one local launchd job at 06:30 plus the same `pull.sh` by hand after practice. Replaces \"no scheduler — run manually\". Still no web server and no auto-email.\n- **Files:** Google Drive only (`00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/`) for raw exports; OneDrive is no longer used.\n\n## Technical Environment\n\n- **OS:** macOS (MacBook, since 2026-08-05) owns the DB and the pull. The Windows laptop is still active but does not write GPS data.\n- **Python:** 3.14 in `gps_report/.venv` (uv)\n- **Languages:** Python (primary), R (available)\n- **Visualization:** Self-contained HTML report (active); Power BI (future/optional)\n- **Constraint:** Baylor IT approval required for cloud-hosted solutions\n\n## Design Constraints\n\n- Nothing that requires significant effort to fix mid-season if it breaks\n- Keep the pipeline transparent and editable without specialized infrastructure knowledge\n- Do not propose ForceDecks or Power BI integration in this project — those are separate\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bc6d97b1-d93e-4d56-9415-7a8b1cd4b578","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:23:44.787Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/CLAUDE.md:\n\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project Purpose\n\nAthletic performance data infrastructure for Baylor University. The primary active project is an automated post-practice GPS report for Football using the Catapult API. ForceDecks integration is a separate, future project.\n\n## Project: `coach_report/`\n\n**Post-session coach report** — high-level planned-vs-actual one-pager for coaches, read-only consumer of `gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` (never writes to it). Sections: planned vs actual (Player Load, PL/min, Explosive Efforts vs day-type historical IQR), max-velocity exposure lists, and XmR SPC flags for over-/under-dosed athletes with sparkline control charts. Output: self-contained HTML + PDF under `coach_report/Reports/coach/YYYY-MM-DD/`.\n\n```\ncd coach_report\npython coach_report.py --date today            # after practice (data must be ingested by gps_report first)\npython coach_report.py --date 2026-04-25       # specific date\npython -m pytest tests/                        # unit tests\n```\n\nDay-type regexes, thresholds, and SPC settings live in `coach_config.yaml`; per-date plan overrides in `plan_overrides.yaml`. Design spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-coach-report-design.md`. Note: the DB column `total_player_load` stores Catapult `average_player_load` (a per-period average; true/stored ratio varies ~5–17× by season — NOT a usable volume metric). coach_report derives **true session Player Load = `player_load_per_minute` × minutes** (verified identical to `pl_low+pl_med+pl_high+pl_veryhigh`, which is the fallback when PL/min is null); this matches AJ's team report exactly. Intensity uses stored `player_load_per_minute` (duration-weighted across multi-session days).\n\n## Active Project: `gps_report/`\n\n**Automated post-practice GPS report** — pulls Football session data from Catapult Connect v6 API, stores summary stats in DuckDB, and generates a self-contained HTML report + plain-text email summary.\n\n### Entry points\n```\ncd gps_report\n\n# Daily report (after practice)\npython run_report.py                          # interactive — picks today's session\npython run_report.py --date 2026-03-10        # specific date\npython run_report.py --session-id <uuid>      # skip picker\npython run_report.py --list-positions         # print Catapult position strings (setup)\npython run_report.py --force                  # re-import existing session\n\n# Regular pull — the one command (also runs daily at 06:30 via launchd com.keystone.gpspull)\n./pull.sh                                     # import new sessions (--since-db), then coach reports for new dates\n\n# Bulk import\npython bulk_import.py --since-db              # newest stored date − pull.overlap_days (3) → today\npython bulk_import.py                         # 2025-03-22 → today (practices, walk-thrus, games, mock games)\npython bulk_import.py --dry-run               # preview matching sessions without DB writes\npython bulk_import.py --start 2025-08-01 --end 2025-12-31\npython bulk_import.py --force                 # re-import sessions already in DB\n\n# Tests (no network, no real DB)\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q\n\n# Backfill / recompute velocity + band columns for historical sessions\npython backfill_velocity.py                   # all non-walk-through sessions\npython backfill_velocity.py --dry-run         # preview without DB writes\npython backfill_velocity.py --session-id <uuid>  # single session\n```\n\n### Session name conventions (Catapult)\n| Type | Name pattern | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Practice | standalone `P` token | `SP25 - P1 - 03.22.25`, `AUBURN - P3 - 08.26.25` |\n| Walk-thru | contains `Walk Thru` | `SP25 - Walk Thru #1 - 03.24.25` |\n| Game | standalone `G` token | `AUBURN - G1 - 08.29.25` |\n| Mock game | contains `Mock Game` → day type `scrimmage` (kept out of practice norms and practice SPC history) | `FC26 - MOCK GAME - 08.29.26` |\n\n### Install dependencies (first time only, macOS)\n```\ncd gps_report\n~/.local/bin/uv venv .venv --python 3.14\n~/.local/bin/uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements-dev.txt\n```\nNever `pip install` globally (Python is PEP 668-managed on this Mac). `pull.sh` and launchd use `gps_report/.venv/bin/python`.\n\n### Regular pull (added 2026-09-13)\n- **Owner:** the Mac owns `data/gps_history.duckdb`. The Windows `Refresh_All_Data` GPS step must stay off (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n- **Schedule:** `ops/com.keystone.gpspull.plist` → `~/Library/LaunchAgents/`, daily 06:30; launchd runs a missed job on wake from sleep, not after power-off. Logs: `gps_report/logs/launchd-gpspull.{log,err}`.\n- **Receipt:** every `bulk_import.py` run writes `logs/last_run.json` (status, exit code, window, counts, `imported_dates`, `last_success_at`). Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 usage/config/token · 2 DB open/lock · 3 partial · 4 all listing windows failed or roster fetch failed · 5 unexpected.\n- **Alerts:** `pull.sh` appends one line to `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` (surfaced at Claude Code session start) on a non-zero import, a coach report that fails or leaves no HTML/PDF, or no successful pull for 36 h.\n- **Atomic sessions:** a session's header and athlete rows commit together or not at all; any stats row without an athlete id fails the session so it is retried.\n- **Retry backlog:** the receipt's `retry_from` is the earliest date of any failed listing window or unstored session. The next `--since-db` run starts at the earlier of `newest − overlap_days` and `retry_from`, so a later success never strands an earlier failure. Only a clean `--since-db` run clears it; range and dry runs never do.\n- Plan and Codex review: `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-PLAN.md`, `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-REVIEW-LOG.md`.\n\n### Key files\n- [gps_report/run_report.py](gps_report/run_report.py) — entry point; session picker, data fetch, report render\n- [gps_report/bulk_import.py](gps_report/bulk_import.py) — bulk historical import (practices, walk-thrus, games)\n- [gps_report/config.yaml](gps_report/config.yaml) — flagging thresholds, position groups, region\n- [gps_report/.env](gps_report/.env) — `CATAPULT_TOKEN=<jwt>` (not in git)\n- [gps_report/src/api_client.py](gps_report/src/api_client.py) — Catapult Connect v6 REST client\n- [gps_report/src/storage.py](gps_report/src/storage.py) — DuckDB schema + queries\n- [gps_report/src/baseline.py](gps_report/src/baseline.py) — rolling 28-day baseline + flagging\n- [gps_report/src/report_builder.py](gps_report/src/report_builder.py) — HTML + email text generation\n- [gps_report/templates/report.html.j2](gps_report/templates/report.html.j2) — Jinja2 report template\n- [gps_report/backfill_velocity.py](gps_report/backfill_velocity.py) — re-fetch and recompute velocity + band columns for historical sessions\n\n### Architecture\n```\nPOST /stats (Catapult Connect v6)\n  └── api_client.py  →  storage.py (DuckDB)\n                              └── baseline.py  →  report_builder.py  →  Reports/YYYY-MM-DD/\n```\n\n### API details (Catapult Connect v6)\n- **Base URL:** `https://connect-us.catapultsports.com/api/v6`\n- **Auth:** JWT Bearer token in `gps_report/.env` as `CATAPULT_TOKEN`\n- **Token scope:** `connect`, `catapultr`, `sensor-read-only`\n- **Activities filter:** `start_time` / `end_time` are **Unix timestamps** (not ISO 8601)\n- **Stats endpoint:** `POST /stats` with `filters: [{name: \"activity_id\", comparison: \"=\", values: [uuid]}]`\n- **Stats source:** `cached_stats`, `group_by: [\"athlete\"]`\n- **`POST /stats` works** and returns 200 — `bake_status=unprocessed` does NOT block it\n- **Do NOT use:** `maximum_velocity`, `high_speed_running_distance`, `athlete_max_velocity`, `percentage_max_velocity`, `deceleration_density` — return 0 or wrong slugs for this account\n- **`max_vel`** = session max velocity in **mph** — multiply × 0.44704 to store as m/s\n- **`velocity_band3_total_distance`** = HSD (75–90% of max vel), in meters\n- **`velocity_band4–8_total_distance`** = sprint bands; bands 5–8 always return 0 for Baylor\n- **Full parameter list** available at `GET /parameters` — 1,829 slugs. Saved to `logs/all_parameters.json`.\n\n### Metric field mapping (API → DB)\n| API field | DB column | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `average_player_load` | `total_player_load` | session average per athlete, not cumulative |\n| `total_distance` | `total_distance_m` | stored in meters; displayed in yards |\n| `max_vel` | `max_velocity_ms` | API value is mph; stored m/s (`× 0.44704`); displayed mph |\n| `velocity_band3_total_distance` | `vb3_distance_m` + `high_speed_distance_m` | raw band stored; derived metric computed from config |\n| `velocity_band4–8_total_distance` | `vb4–vb8_distance_m` + `sprint_distance_m` | raw bands stored; derived metric summed from config |\n| `velocity_band3/4_total_effort_count` | `vb3_effort_count`, `vb4_effort_count` | # entries into HSD/sprint zones |\n| `acceleration_density` | `accel_density` | |\n| `explosive_efforts` | `explosive_efforts` | = `total_high_ima` (same values) |\n| `total_duration` | `total_duration_s` | session duration in seconds |\n| `total_acceleration_load` | `total_accel_load` | |\n| `average_velocity` | `average_velocity_ms` | stored m/s |\n| `meterage_per_minute` | `meterage_per_minute` | |\n| `player_load_per_minute` | `player_load_per_minute` | |\n| `explosive_ratio_(avg)` | `explosive_ratio_avg` | |\n| `ima_band3_accel/decel/right/left_count` | `ima_high_accel/decel/right/left` | high-intensity IMA counts |\n| `high_ima_accel/decel` | `ima_high_accel_decel` | combined high IMA accel+decel |\n| `total_high/medium/low_ima(_movements)` | `total_high/medium/low_ima` | IMA movement tier totals |\n| `ima/min`, `total_high_ima/min`, `total_high_ima_(avg)` | `ima_per_minute`, `total_high_ima_per_min`, `total_high_ima_avg` | IMA rate/avg metrics |\n| `impacts_low/med/high` | `impacts_low/med/high` | collision/contact event counts |\n| `impact_low_(avg)`, `impacts_med_(avg)`, `impacts_high_(avg)` | `impacts_low/med/high_avg` | impact averages |\n| `pl_low/med/high/veryhigh` | `pl_low/med/high/veryhigh` | player load band totals |\n| `pl_med_(avg)` | `pl_high_avg` | ⚠️ Catapult name/slug mismatch — slug says \"med\" but value is PL_High (Avg) |\n| `pl_veryhigh_(avg)`, `pl_veryhigh/min` | `pl_veryhigh_avg`, `pl_veryhigh_per_min` | |\n| `total_lineman_contact_count` | `total_contacts` | all players (not just linemen despite name) |\n| `total_qb_throw_count` | `total_throws` | QB-specific; zero for all non-QB athletes |\n\n### Velocity band storage architecture\nRaw band columns (`vb3_distance_m`–`vb8_distance_m`) are stored as DB ground truth. Derived metrics (`high_speed_distance_m`, `sprint_distance_m`) are computed at ingest from `config.yaml` `metrics.derived` band assignments — same principle as m→yds/m/s→mph unit conversions. To redefine HSD or Sprint zones: edit `config.yaml` → run `python backfill_velocity.py`. No code changes needed.\n\n### Athlete roster API fields (`GET /athletes`)\n- **Name:** `first_name` + `last_name` (separate fields — no `full_name`, `name`, or `displayName`)\n- **Jersey:** `jersey` field (string, may be non-numeric e.g. `\"DBB\"`) — parse to `int`, store `NULL` if non-numeric\n- **Position:** `position_name` (e.g. `\"DL\"`) preferred over `position` (single-letter code e.g. `\"D\"`)\n- Parsed in `parse_athlete()` in both `run_report.py` and `bulk_import.py`\n\n### Position group mapping\nRun `--list-positions` to see actual Catapult position strings. Config already updated with live values from web UI. Position names from `GET /athletes` include `position_name` field.\n\n### HTML report layout (sections, top to bottom)\n1. Header band (Baylor green) — wordmark, session name/date, athlete count\n2. Gold accent bar\n3. KPI tiles (4) — Team Avg PL · Avg Distance (yds) · Avg Max Speed mph (N/A when 0) · Avg Explosive Efforts\n4. Charts row — SVG volume trend sparkline (last 10 sessions) + Top Speeds CSS bars (top 8 by mph)\n5. Position Group Summary table — group, N, avg PL, avg dist (yds), avg speed (mph), avg HSD (yds), avg explosive; high/low cell shading\n6. Athlete Flags — card layout per athlete, HIGH (orange) / LOW (blue) badges with baseline context\n7. Offensive Breakdown — Skill, OL group player tables\n8. Defensive Breakdown — DBs, STAR, LB, DL group player tables\n9. Other — Special Teams\n10. Footer\n\n### Display units\n- **Distance:** stored in meters (DB), displayed in **yards** everywhere in report (`m_to_yds()` in `src/utils.py`)\n- **Velocity:** stored in m/s (DB), displayed in **mph** everywhere in report (`ms_to_mph()` in `src/utils.py`)\n- Do NOT change DB storage units — conversion is display-layer only\n\n### Baseline flagging\n- Activates after 3 sessions per athlete (configurable: `flagging.min_sessions_for_baseline`)\n- Default: flag if value is >1.5 SD from rolling 28-day personal average\n- Metrics flagged: Total Player Load, Total Distance, High Speed Distance\n\n### Jinja2 + pandas NA gotcha\nPandas `NA` values (from DuckDB nullable integer columns like `jersey_number`) cannot be evaluated as booleans in Jinja2 (`{% if athlete.jersey_number %}`). Always convert with `None if pd.isna(val) else val` in `report_builder.py` before passing to the template.\n\n### DuckDB lock risk\n`data/gps_history.duckdb` allows one writer. A second writer (a manual `run_report.py` or import during the 06:30 pull) fails fast with a lock error — the import exits 2 and alerts. Never put the DB in a cloud-synced folder (Google Drive / OneDrive sync locks it); it stays local and gitignored.\n\n## Architecture Decisions\n\n- **Scope:** Football GPS only — ForceDecks is a separate future project\n- **Storage:** DuckDB local file (`gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb`) — summary stats only, no raw 10Hz data\n- **API:** Catapult Connect v6 (US region); JWT token in `gps_report/.env`\n- **Scheduled pull (changed 2026-09-13, Eric):** one local launchd job at 06:30 plus the same `pull.sh` by hand after practice. Replaces \"no scheduler — run manually\". Still no web server and no auto-email.\n- **Files:** Google Drive only (`00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/`) for raw exports; OneDrive is no longer used.\n\n## Technical Environment\n\n- **OS:** macOS (MacBook, since 2026-08-05) owns the DB and the pull. The Windows laptop is still active but does not write GPS data.\n- **Python:** 3.14 in `gps_report/.venv` (uv)\n- **Languages:** Python (primary), R (available)\n- **Visualization:** Self-contained HTML report (active); Power BI (future/optional)\n- **Constraint:** Baylor IT approval required for cloud-hosted solutions\n\n## Design Constraints\n\n- Nothing that requires significant effort to fix mid-season if it breaks\n- Keep the pipeline transparent and editable without specialized infrastructure knowledge\n- Do not propose ForceDecks or Power BI integration in this project — those are separate\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
