{"parentUuid":"e978f768-c8a0-4487-a20c-be7a5b3e1078","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf84NMCm3VUYbh8Z3kRio","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VheoT4DwFqANjajUE3ceZZ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","old_string":"- Rewrite git history to drop `API_Token_FB.txt`? Eric's call (repo is private).\n","new_string":"- Rewrite git history to drop `API_Token_FB.txt`? Eric's call (repo is private).\n\n## Gotchas\n- **A NameResolution / \"Can't assign requested address\" error at 06:30 usually means the Mac was asleep,\n  not that Catapult or DNS is down.** On battery, launchd runs the missed 06:30 job during a 2-second\n  DarkWake (a brief background wake with no usable Wi-Fi). The process then freezes between wakes, and\n  the 2/4/8s retries all land in one dead window. 2026-09-16: started 06:48, failed 07:24, Wi-Fi\n  `E_CONNECTION_LOSS` at 07:07. Confirm with `pmset -g log | grep -E \"DarkWake|Sleep \"` around the run\n  time, then just rerun `pull.sh`. Do not lengthen the API client's backoff; it would freeze across\n  sleeps too and delay real-outage alerts.\n- A manual catch-up run also writes a `stale` alert line first (it checks the 36 h gap before importing).\n  That line is expected when recovering from a missed morning.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7047,"cache_read_input_tokens":143746,"output_tokens":1424,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":79},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7047,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1424,"cache_read_input_tokens":143746,"cache_creation_inpu