{"parentUuid":"133c2d92-ae5f-4a1a-bc56-cb5a0d67ef97","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f7ce738b-a84e-4a4f-9b40-8b6a0448090a","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:23:58.687Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f7ce738b-a84e-4a4f-9b40-8b6a0448090a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf84PNnntRqiT731MwFxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recovered today's missed GPS data. Nothing needed fixing in the code, Catapult, or DNS. The pull failed only because the Mac was asleep.\n\n**Why it failed:** The Mac was asleep on battery at 06:30. macOS started the missed job during a 2-second background wake with no usable Wi-Fi. The Mac then went back to sleep in the middle of the run, so every retry failed. The runs on 9/14 and 9/15 worked at 06:30, and the Catapult address resolves fine now.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Pull:** I ran `pull.sh` by hand. It imported 2 new sessions (09-15, 09-16), skipped 3 it already had, and had 0 errors. Coach reports (HTML and PDF) were built for both dates. The data is now current to 2026-09-16.\n- **Notes:** I wrote the cause and how to spot it into `docs/STATUS.md`. Commit `9ae7f5d`, pushed.\n- **Alert log:** It has a new \"stale\" GPS line. That is normal after a missed morning, because the script checks the gap before it imports. I left the old 07:24 line too.\n\n**You need to decide:** Should the Mac wake up for the 06:30 pull?\n1. **Wake it (my pick).** Leave the Mac plugged in overnight, then run this once:\n   `! sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 06:28:00`\n   The pull then runs on time with working Wi-Fi.\n2. **Leave it.** On a morning when the Mac is asleep, you get one alert line. Run `pull.sh` by hand or wait for the next 06:30 run. No data is lost.\n\nAlso, `STATUS.md` in this repo still has an empty `.from-windows` block at the end. I did not remove it. Say if you want it gone.\n\nresult: Recovered today's GPS data (2 new sessions, coach reports built). The failure was the Mac sleeping on battery, not Catapult or the code (repo commit `9ae7f5d`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_read_input_tokens":150793,"output_tokens":677,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":150793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf84PNHn1hGQL4Nu2FTKd","type":"assistant","uuid":"507075a7-f2c1-4f7c-9c30-25b57a8af151","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:24:05.511Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
