{"parentUuid":"a9c429df-dacf-4d83-95a1-b8ef49137a0b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","snippet":"44\t  not that Catapult or DNS is down.** On battery, launchd runs the missed 06:30 job during a 2-second\n45\t  DarkWake (a brief background wake with no usable Wi-Fi). The process then freezes between wakes, and\n46\t  the 2/4/8s retries all land in one dead window. 2026-09-16: started 06:48, failed 07:24, Wi-Fi\n47\t  `E_CONNECTION_LOSS` at 07:07. Confirm with `pmset -g log | grep -E \"DarkWake|Sleep \"` around the run\n48\t  time, then just rerun `pull.sh`. Do not lengthen the API client's backoff; it would freeze across\n49\t  sleeps too and delay real-outage alerts.\n50\t- A manual catch-up run also writes a `stale` alert line first (it checks the 36 h gap before importing).\n51\t  That line is expected when recovering from a missed morning."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1644e7c8-5160-4773-9924-bf702e438794","timestamp":"2026-09-17T00:26:11.800Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n44\t  not that Catapult or DNS is down.** On battery, launchd runs the missed 06:30 job during a 2-second\n45\t  DarkWake (a brief background wake with no usable Wi-Fi). The process then freezes between wakes, and\n46\t  the 2/4/8s retries all land in one dead window. 2026-09-16: started 06:48, failed 07:24, Wi-Fi\n47\t  `E_CONNECTION_LOSS` at 07:07. Confirm with `pmset -g log | grep -E \"DarkWake|Sleep \"` around the run\n48\t  time, then just rerun `pull.sh`. Do not lengthen the API client's backoff; it would freeze across\n49\t  sleeps too and delay real-outage alerts.\n50\t- A manual catch-up run also writes a `stale` alert line first (it checks the 36 h gap before importing).\n51\t  That line is expected when recovering from a missed morning.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting","sessionId":"b4e73986-d9fe-48ee-8449-471485f44b0e","version":"2.1.273","gitBranch":"main"}
