{"parentUuid":"cb22aee7-5c70-404b-b792-0c5d04d0e565","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf85yUioXPcxfqezsKnwH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The backup ran, but it ended with one error that needs your decision.\n\n- **What worked:** All 86 jobs ran. CRASHBOX was plugged in, so the SSD got everything, including files that are not committed. GitHub pushes, Drive copies, and both receipts all passed. The memsearch index finished too (261 chunks).\n- **The error:** `Weekly_Research_Review` is not listed in `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json`. The backup counts any DEV folder not on that list as an error. The folder was already backed up in this run. The error only means it has no class yet.\n- **Why I stopped:** The manifest says a person must pick the class. Yesterday you also corrected me when I guessed a class from a repo's name.\n\nPick one class for `Weekly_Research_Review`:\n1. **Institutional (my pick).** It is a weekly paper review for Baylor staff: decks, a Teams post, and an email. It gets backed up to the SSD, GitHub, and `baylor`. The `baylor` target is turned off, so in practice this is the same as personal.\n2. **Personal.** It gets backed up to the SSD and GitHub. This is how the 6 repos from yesterday were set.\n\nWhen you answer, I will add the repo to the manifest, commit and push `~/.claude`, and run the backup again. Once that run passes, I will archive the error line so it stops showing up at session start.\n\nneeds input: Should `Weekly_Research_Review` be **institutional** or **personal** in the backup manifest?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1353,"cache_read_input_tokens":176585,"output_tokens":717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":217},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephem