{"parentUuid":"201281b9-a1fb-4d3f-af45-df8806010133","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"692bdd65-5242-4a98-97af-3abdde2a6da2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0154fWDHjDEcyYkPKxzyQh9s","type":"tool_result","content":"## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n7d5cc55 Merge pull request #1 from erash11/router/weekly-research-review","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"56f1cdcc-9fd3-4604-8a3d-0cbdfef60adb","timestamp":"2026-09-17T01:05:49.688Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n7d5cc55 Merge pull request #1 from erash11/router/weekly-research-review","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/COMMANDS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":424,"oldLines":6,"newStart":424,"newLines":7,"lines":[" |---|---|---|"," | `/status-report` | Every 2 weeks | Kenny + Chris email, one-page PDF, internal record |"," | `/weekly-review` | Weekly | Week in review |","+| `/research-in-5` or \"Research in 5 on this paper: <PDF / DOI / Zotero item>\" | Weekly | 5-slide deck (dark + light PDF) for Teams, Teams post, email, index row. Runs from `DEV/Weekly_Research_Review`; PDF export on Windows only |"," | `/project-triage` | Weekly | DEV/ triage HTML dashboard |"," | `/claude-stack-doctor` | Monday | Full automation health check |"," | `/closeout` | End of day | Sign-off sweep. Commits, memory, handoff |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":6,"newStart":10,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `SportScienceResearchRepo/` | Main research repo. Has `CONTEXT.md`, a spec sheet, and an `index.html` micro-app → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `ZoteroInjestion/` | Zotero ingest pipeline (~1,850 files). Note the spelling — \"Injestion\", not \"Ingestion\". |"," | `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |","+| `Weekly_Research_Review/` | \"Research in 5\": weekly one-paper review. Deck PDF for Teams, post, email, running index. Outputs on `_DRIVE/07_EDUCATION/Research_in_5` → own `AGENTS.md` |"," | `Epilepsy-Baseball-Research/` | Epilepsy + baseball literature review |"," | `BookInbox/` | Staging for books not yet ingested |"," | `reMarkale_extract/` | reMarkable highlight extraction. Note the spelling — \"reMarkale\". |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":11,"newStart":1,"newLines":13,"lines":[" # STATUS — ~/DEV workspace root"," "," ## Current state","+- 2026-09-14 Windows closeout: all 144 discovered DEV repos are clean against their recorded upstreams. Migration items 2-4 and 6 are complete; detailed handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-windows-migration-closeout.md`."," - 2026-09-14 (Mac): `/doctor-plus` context audit. 40 owned skills set `name-only` in `~/.claude/settings.json`; step/analysis logs moved out of Risk_Stratification_Engine and Ath_Medicine guidance files; FaceComps and PlayCalls `CLAUDE.md` now `@AGENTS.md`. Detail: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-doctor-plus-context-audit.md`."," - 2026-09-14 migration closed out. Every DEV project repo has a GitHub remote under erash11, all clean and pushed. Duplicate clone folders (`Gemini Projects`, `Website`) moved to `_to_delete/2026-09-14_dup_clones/`."," - Cowork project migration is COMPLETE. All cloud projects point at their disk repo from the project instructions block; WebApps, PlayerProfiles and Post Season Analysis were the last three and are archived."," - Codex scratch in `~/Documents/Codex` swept. Salvage went to PP_Recruiting, Baylor_Doc_Style, TechEd_Prop, agent-skills, and `_DRIVE/00_INBOX/Personal`. That folder now carries `_SAFE_TO_DELETE.md` (3.2 GB, left in place by choice).","-- Recovered scripts re-filed 2026-09-14: `ZoteroInjestion/scripts/prepare_publication_syntheses.py` and `CLI_Dev/codex-win-to-mac-migration/`. Two of the five were byte-identical duplicates of scripts already tracked in dotclaude `skills-archive/2026-07-24-os-audit/` and were dropped. Holding folder retired to `_to_delete/2026-09-14_recovered-from-codex/`.","+- Recovered scripts re-filed 2026-09-14: the superseded publication utility is archived at `ZoteroInjestion/scripts/legacy/prepare_publication_syntheses.py`, and the migration tool and tests live at `CLI_Dev/codex-win-to-mac-migration/`. The other two utilities were byte-identical to existing local-pool scripts and were not overwritten. The complete holding folder remains recoverable at `_to_delete/2026-09-14_recovered-from-codex/`.","+- The guarded Windows v2 skill sync is complete. `~/.claude/skills` is the pushed canonical repo; `~/.agents/skills` and `~/.codex/skills` are generated copy views with 40 identical managed entries and preserved third-party/view-only skills. Platform-specific path configs preserve Mac behavior and supply Windows paths."," - Security: a historical VALD client secret surfaced during the migration audit. Current working files and migration artifacts were redacted, but the old value remains in private Git history and must be rotated."," - The thin workspace router is synced with GitHub."," - 2026-09-14 (Mac): stack doctor + dev-sync done. All 138 DEV repos clean and pushed on the Mac. Cloned the six repos Windows created (PP_Recruiting, PythonScripts_2024, RTP_ProgressReport, VALD_Release, Supervisor_Reviews, VALD_Performance) plus `SpecialRequests/Zinnecker_Skylar`, and gave the six router rows. `~/DEV/Claude outputs` docx files moved to `_DRIVE/02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/04_Outputs/`. Detail: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-mac-stack-doctor-dev-sync.md`."]},{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":24,"newStart":20,"newLines":22,"lines":[" - Next session: confirm every listed skill shows a description (skill listing budget is ~30,000 chars; predicted ~26,800)."," - Rotate the exposed VALD client secret, then verify the replacement is stored outside Git and project documentation."," - Delete `~/Documents/Codex` when ready. 3.2 GB, nothing in it that is not already in git.","-- Prepare Windows for the guarded v2 skills sync."," - Write lesson 0002 in RTP_Constraints_Course and import its 122 Myszka references into Zotero."," - Run the next Baylor forecast capture on Wednesday, 2026-09-16.","-- Eyeball the 36 real `.from-windows` conflict files, mostly in Ath_Medicine/.","-- Let `daily-backup` run once clean (09:00 or `/backup`); consolidate `USER.md` (95%) and `MEMORY.md` (101%) before the next memory write.","+- Consolidate `USER.md` (95%) and `MEMORY.md` (101%) before the next memory write."," - Decide whether `RTP_WorkingGroup/RTP_ProgressREPORT/` or the new `RTP_ProgressReport` repo is current.","+- Confirm that `Ath_Medicine`, `Baylor_Exposure_Data`, and `Risk_Stratification_Engine` contain no identifiable athlete or health data that should remain local-only.","+- On the Mac, pull `~/.claude/skills` and run its guarded sync so the Mac-generated views receive the same canonical revision."," "," ## Open questions"," - Turn off the `last30days` plugin? 0 uses since 2026-08-05.","-- Publish `claude-skills` as a marketplace so Codex pulls all 47 skills by git instead of hand-copies? Decide scope first: all 47, or split portable from Claude-Code-only (harvest, memory-write, claude-stack-doctor need CC hooks). Unconfirmed whether it reaches Cowork."," - Has the exposed VALD client secret been revoked and replaced?","-- Which copy of ZoteroInjestion is the live one: top level or LibraryProject/?","-- LibraryProject.code-workspace still points at SportScienceResearchRepo, which now lives in _ARCHIVE/.","+- `LibraryProject.code-workspace` points at a nonexistent nested `SportScienceResearchRepo`; the live repo is at the DEV root."," "," ## Gotchas"," - `skillOverrides` does not apply to plugin skills. A plugin is on or off as a whole.","-- `~/.codex/skills` is NOT a git repo. Its overlap with claude-skills is hand-copied and drifts; 5 of 9 shared skills had already diverged as of 2026-09-14. Edit both copies until the marketplace fix lands.","-- `LibraryProject` carries `ZoteroInjestion` as a submodule. Committing to ZoteroInjestion leaves LibraryProject dirty until the pointer is bumped.","+- `~/.agents/skills` and `~/.codex/skills` are generated views, not authoring locations. Edit and push `~/.claude/skills`, then run the platform sync; do not hand-edit managed copies.","+- The top-level `ZoteroInjestion` checkout is the working clone. `LibraryProject` carries the same repo as a submodule and currently pins the same `10e3986` commit; later Zotero commits require a submodule-pointer bump there."," - Keep the `/*` rule in `.gitignore`."," - If every pull fails with \"Another git process seems to be running\", look for zero-byte `.git/*.lock` files left by an interrupted run (138 on 2026-09-14; search deeper than depth 4, submodules keep theirs under `.git/modules/`). Move them aside, never delete."," - Each project folder is its own Git repo."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-windows-migration-closeout.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":137,"lines":["+# Windows migration closeout — 2026-09-14","+","+## What was worked on and why","+","+Closed the Windows side of the GitHub and Google Drive migration items Eric delegated: resolve `_INBOX`, publish a guarded cross-harness skill system, place recovered Codex utilities in canonical homes, and correct migration status documents. The goal was to leave the application workspace safe to continue from a terminal with Claude Code or Codex without hand-copied skill drift or undiscoverable scratch-only tools.","+","+## Decisions and reasoning","+","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills` is the Git-backed canonical skill source. Managed entries in `.agents` and `.codex` are generated copies; locally installed non-managed skills remain untouched.","+- Shared skill paths are split into macOS and Windows JSON files. The selector has no machine paths. This preserves Mac behavior without publishing Mac-only paths into Windows callers.","+- The Windows SecondBrain path is declared but absent. Vault-backed meeting sync fails clearly rather than creating an empty substitute vault.","+- Three useful verification gates from the old agents view were merged into canonical. The richer canonical Impeccable tree was retained, with only five missing compatible provider files added.","+- The first real sync exposed legacy regular files tracked below three paths that are now local junctions. Both sync twins now use recursive index-only removal and check the native Git exit code. The links remain on disk and Git contains no mode-120000 entries.","+- Recovered utilities were placed by ownership. The obsolete Zotero publication script remains archival and inactive; two exact duplicates were not overwritten.","+- Repeated memory-compiler `error result: success` failures were confirmed as SDK/bundled-CLI version skew. Updating `claude-agent-sdk` 0.2.110 to 0.2.152 restored compilation. Two malformed knowledge links were corrected; structural lint now has zero errors.","+","+## Verification completed","+","+- Full DEV sweep: 144 repositories, zero dirty or recorded ahead/behind states.","+- Skill views: two identical 40-entry manifests; 568 managed-file comparisons; zero hash drift; no managed reparse points; 266 non-managed agents entries and 24 non-managed Codex entries preserved.","+- Rollback copies exist in Google Drive and `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.agents\\skills-archive\\pre-sync-2026-09-14-215006`.","+- Recovered utilities: five SHA-256 matches; migration suite six of six passed; Zotero legacy source compiles.","+- Memory: pending session-end queue empty; today transcript current; all daily logs compiled; structural lint zero errors; refreshed search index at 12,746 chunks with targeted migration retrieval succeeding.","+","+## Git commits","+","+- DEV router: `bf5993f` plus this closeout commit.","+- `_INBOX`: `325a6c5` (following hardening commits through `e2df8bd`).","+- `claude-skills`: `2c655e9`, `98f7517`, `850b1b3`.","+- `CLI_Dev`: `cdb1bcd`, `f3e72cf`.","+- `ZoteroInjestion`: `10e3986`, `a38bc94`.","+- `agent-skills`: `4cf5670`, `371583b`.","+- `claude-memory-compiler`: `98ef319` (includes the SDK recovery and the current upstream merge).","+- `dotclaude`: `8cfd300` (includes the Windows transcript capture and the current upstream merge).","+- `claude-global-memory`: `47c1f48` (preserves both the Windows flush and the concurrent upstream transcript capture).","+","+## Exact file inventory","+","+### DEV and session reports","+","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\docs\\STATUS.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\docs\\handoffs\\2026-09-14-windows-migration-closeout.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\_INBOX\\docs\\STATUS.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\.gitignore`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\progress.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\task-W2-brief.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\task-W2-report.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\task-W3-brief.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\KeystoneOS\\.superpowers\\sdd\\2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios\\task-W3-report.md`","+","+### Canonical skills and clone-local safeguards","+","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills\\_shared\\config.json`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills\\_shared\\config.macos.json`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills\\_shared\\config.windows.json`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills\\_shared\\README.md`","+- `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\skills\\capture-insigh